Z||000000||JC Webb||10-23-2000||07:52 PM||||<BR>I plan on replacing the ignition system on my 86 SE V-6 with a Crane HI-6S.  Has anyone done this before?  Does anyone suggest a better system?  Thank you for your time and response!||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-24-2000||09:07 AM||||I had a Crane Hi-6S in my 86 SE 4spd Nitrous. and it worked great but the MSD 6AL showed more improvement on the dyno. but if the price is right GET IT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and it takes about 2 hours to do including hiding all the wires for a show quality install...<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-24-2000||09:34 AM||||Would an upgrade like that eliminate the hassle of changing the pick-up coil on an annual basis?  I was wondering if it replaces that part of the system.  That things stranded me a couple of times.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-24-2000||07:31 PM||||I beleive all the aftermarket addon units use the stock HEI parts in the distributor. Both the pickup and module are retained. The aftermarket cap discharge boxes live between the module and the coil. There are a couple companies making "improved" modules but none I know of replaces the pickup. (I once heard of an optical conversion but have never seen it done on HEI distributor.)||||reg||1
